@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "All features: remote access and job cards";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Everything in one subscription: branded remote support and remote access, job cards and ticketing, monthly health checks, a knowledge base and live chat.";
}
<section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h1>All features</h1>
        <p class="lede">Everything is in every full-version subscription — there are no add-ons and no per-computer prices.</p>
        <div class="next-links"><partial name="_SiteCta" /></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid2">
        <div class="card">
            <h2 style="margin-top:0"><a href="/remote-support">Remote support</a></h2>
            <ul class="feature-list" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
                <li>Request Support rings every technician</li>
                <li>Unattended access, the customer's switch and password</li>
                <li>Every monitor, H.264, their real pointer</li>
                <li>Files and copy-and-paste both ways; drag and drop</li>
                <li>Printing both ways; talking and their sound</li>
                <li>Ctrl+Alt+Del, admin prompts, restart and reconnect</li>
                <li>Privacy screen and session recording</li>
                <li>Running programs and performance without connecting</li>
                <li>Help from outside, with the customer's code</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h2 style="margin-top:0"><a href="/ticketing">Job cards and ticketing</a></h2>
            <ul class="feature-list" style="grid-template-columns:1fr">
                <li>A ticket for every session, with its time</li>
                <li>Workshop, call-out, walk-in, remote and general routes</li>
                <li>Photos in and out, damage reports, delivery</li>
                <li>Quote requests to suppliers, signed</li>
                <li>Recurring tasks that open their own tickets</li>
                <li>A billing queue for the office</li>
                <li>Tickets by email and a contact form</li>
                <li>Client updates by email, replies on the ticket</li>
                <li>Several people per ticket, @@mentions, office chat</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h2 style="margin-top:0"><a href="/health-checks">Monthly health checks</a></h2>
            <p>Disks, backups, updates, security and Windows 11 readiness for every computer, with the housekeeping done, in one report per client.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h2 style="margin-top:0"><a href="/knowledge-base">Knowledge base</a></h2>
            <p>Written from the ticket that solved it, general or per client, with folders, pictures and every version kept.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h2 style="margin-top:0"><a href="/website-chat">Live chat and browser support</a></h2>
            <p>A chat bubble and a contact form for your website, and screen sharing in a browser for someone with nothing installed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h2 style="margin-top:0"><a href="/security">Security</a></h2>
            <p>End-to-end encrypted sessions, two-factor sign-in for everybody, and your data in South Africa.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h2 style="margin-top:0">Your brand</h2>
            <p>Your logo, colours and name on the customer's app, prompts, download page, installer, emails and your technicians' console — changed once in the portal, everywhere.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
            <h2 style="margin-top:0">Your team</h2>
            <p>Owner, supervisor, technician and office administrator — tick what each person needs. Light or dark, each person's own; the portal works on a phone.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
